This product includes software and ideas developed by third parties.
The implementation in this repository is original; the items below are
acknowledged as prior art or as algorithmic inspiration.

1. SplitMix64
   Deterministic pseudo-random generator by Guy L. Steele Jr., Doug Lea,
   Christine H. Flood (2014). Public-domain algorithm; reimplemented here
   in about twenty lines in rng.mbt.

2. Hadamard's well-posedness conditions
   Existence, uniqueness and stability of solutions, as formulated by
   Jacques Hadamard. Used as the conceptual basis of the three checks in
   verify.mbt. No code is derived from any source.

3. Vieta's formulas
   Textbook mathematics; used in family_quadratic.mbt to derive
   coefficients from a declared pair of roots.

4. QuickCheck
   Property-based testing with shrinking, originally by Koen Claessen and
   John Hughes. Not reimplemented here: kiln uses MoonBit's standard
   library (@quickcheck) where property tests are appropriate.

5. Finite-domain regression (0.2)
   Backtracking, minimum remaining values, forward checking, symmetric set
   difference, Hamming distance and deletion-based conflict checks are standard
   techniques. The code is an original implementation, not a new algorithm claim.

